      <div class="seo-answer"><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Informed consent at Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic means explaining the proposed treatment, its benefits, risks and alternatives, and obtaining your voluntary agreement before care begins; you may withdraw consent at any time.</div>
<nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Consent Notice</li></ol></nav>

    <section class="hero-section">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Consent Notice</h1>
        <p class="lead">This notice explains what you agree to when you submit an enquiry or appointment request. Mind Grace uses the contact information you provide for appointment coordination and care-related communication.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <div class="container narrow">
        <article class="legal-content">
          <h2>Information we collect</h2>
          <p>When you submit an enquiry or appointment request through our website, we collect the following information:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your name and contact details (phone number, email address)</li>
            <li>Preferred appointment date and time</li>
            <li>Brief description of your concern (optional)</li>
            <li>Any specific doctor preference</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>How we use your information</h2>
          <p>Your information is used solely for:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Scheduling and confirming appointments</li>
            <li>Communicating about your care</li>
            <li>Sending appointment reminders</li>
            <li>Responding to your enquiries</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Your Consent</h2>
          <p>By submitting your information through this website, you consent to the limited appointment-coordination uses described below. Do not submit emergency details or a detailed medical history through the public website, email, or WhatsApp.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Dr. Anita Sharma and Mind Grace Clinic staff using your contact information for appointment coordination</li>
            <li>Receiving phone calls, SMS, or emails related to your appointment</li>
            <li>Handling of the submitted details through the clinic and booking systems in use, subject to the safeguards and retention practices described in the Privacy Notice</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Confidentiality Assurance</h2>
          <p>All patient information is treated with strict confidentiality in accordance with:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The Mental Healthcare Act, 2017</li>
            <li>RCI (Rehabilitation Council of India) guidelines</li>
            <li>Medical council ethical guidelines</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Website Content Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>The content on this website is for educational and informational purposes only. It is not a substitute for:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Professional medical diagnosis</li>
            <li>Personalized treatment recommendations</li>
            <li>Emergency medical care</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Always consult with a qualified healthcare provider for any health concerns.</p>

          <h2>Your Rights</h2>
          <p>You have the right to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Access your personal information held by the clinic</li>
            <li>Request corrections to inaccurate information</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent for non-essential communications</li>
            <li>Request deletion of your data subject to legal requirements</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Contact Us</h2>
          <p>If you have questions about this consent notice or how we handle your information, please contact us:</p>
          <address>
            Mind Grace Neuropsychiatric Clinic<br>
            J123, Gamma II, Greater Noida, 201310<br>
            Phone: +91 96678 63295<br>
            Email: contact@mindgracencr.in
          </address>

          <p class="last-updated"><em>Last updated: January 2024</em></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
